{"test_id": "B23-020", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B23", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP requirements align with PDPA obligations for data breach notification?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CCoP CSA notification has different (often shorter) timeline", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "PDPA requires assessment before notification with affected party notification", "tier": "critical", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}, {"fact": "Affected party notification is PDPA-specific requirement", "tier": "important", "source": "Multi-regulatory framework: government"}], "expected_response": "CCoP 2.0 does not set MAS, PDPC or other external reporting timelines in the Code itself. The grounded position is that the CIIO must maintain the incident-reporting structure required by the CCoP for the designated CII and separately comply with each external reporting regime that applies to the scenario. Where timelines differ, the CIIO should design its internal process to meet the applicable obligations in parallel, document the mapping between regimes, and escalate any irreconcilable conflict under its cybersecurity risk-management framework and, where necessary, through the waiver or guidance process. Reference: CCoP 2.0 §1.6, §3.2.1, §7.1.1(b); Cybersecurity Act 2018 §11(7).", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify regulatory frameworks involved", "Analyze alignment type: complementary_notification_obligations", "Map overlapping and distinct requirements"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating one regulator completely replaces another", "Assuming alignment without checking for conflicts", "Downplaying regulator-specific requirements", "Clear articulation of regulatory alignment or conflict", "Coordination strategy for overlapping requirements", "Reference to specific regulatory frameworks"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific regulatory provisions", "Creating non-existent regulatory overlaps"]}, "metadata": {"section": "N/A (multi-regulator coordination is not addressed in CCoP 2.0; remove or set to null)", "clause_reference": ["1.6.1", "1.6.2", "1.6.3", "3.2.1", "7.1.1(b)"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "regulatory_coordination", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Cybersecurity Act 2018 §11(7)"]}}
